  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $476$\n\nII. $732$\n\nIII. $423$",
  "worked_solution": "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $476,$ we have that \n\n$$\n47-2(6)=47-12=35\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $476$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $732,$ we have that \n\n$$\n73-2(2)=73-4=69\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $732$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $423,$ we have that \n\n$$\n42-2(3)=42-6=36\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $423$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
